NIGERIA BELONGS TO JESUS CHRIST
The 1st Commandment:


I am the Lord your God! You shall have no other gods before me!


Whoever can read these words correctly will probably see in them the judgment of many who do not observe this most important of all commandments.


"You shall have no other gods!"


Many people do not imagine enough of these words. They have made it too easy for themselves! When they think of idolaters, they probably only think of those people who kneel before a row of wooden figures, each of which represents a particular god. They may also think of devil worshippers and other such misguided people, whom they think of with pity at best, but they do not think of themselves.


Just take a look and see if you belong there!


One has a child who is truly more important to him than anything else, for whom he would make any sacrifice, forgetting everything else. Another places earthly pleasure far above everything else, and even with the best will in the world would not be able to give up this pleasure for anything if he were faced with such a demand that he could make a voluntary decision. A third loves money, a fourth loves power, a fifth loves a woman, another loves earthly distinction, and in all of this, all of them ultimately only love themselves!


This is idolatry in the truest sense. The first commandment warns against it and forbids it! And woe to those who do not follow it literally!


This transgression immediately takes its revenge in that such a person must always remain earthbound when he passes over into the subtle realm. In reality, however, he has only earthbound himself through his attachment to something that is on earth! He is thus prevented from further ascent, loses the time granted to him for this and runs the risk of not leaving the subtle realm in time in a resurrection from it to the bright realm of the free spirits.


Then he is swept away into the inevitable decomposition of all materiality, which serves to purify it for its resurrection and its new formation. But this is the spiritual death of all personal consciousness for the human soul and thus also the destruction of its form and its name for eternity!


The observance of the commandment is meant to protect us from this terrible thing! It is the most important commandment because it is one of the most necessary for man! Unfortunately, man is far too prone to giving in to some inclination that ultimately enslaves him! But what he allows to become an inclination he turns into a golden calf, which he puts in the highest place and thus also as an idol or deity next to his God, and very often even above him!


Unfortunately, there are all too many "inclinations" that man has created for himself and which he is happy to adopt with the greatest carelessness! Inclinations are a preference for something earthly, as I have already mentioned. There are of course many more.


But whoever acquires a tendency that "hangs," as the word correctly expresses it, is thereby attached to the material world when he enters the beyond for his further development, and cannot easily break free from it, and is thus inhibited, held back! One could even call it a curse that remains upon him. The process is the same, no matter how it is expressed literally.


However, if he places God above everything in his earthly existence, not only in his imagination or only in words, but in his feelings, that is, truly and genuinely, in reverent love that binds him as if to a slope, then through this bond he will immediately strive further upwards with the same effect when he enters the afterlife; for he takes the veneration and love of God with him, it holds him and carries him ultimately to paradise, the abode of pure spirits freed from all burdens, whose bond only leads to God's luminous truth!


Therefore, be sure to strictly observe this commandment. This will protect you from many unfavorable twists of fate.


